From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:01:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] swiotlb: make the wrappers' calls dead code without
 CONFIG_SWIOTLB

swiotlb_tbl_unmap_single(), swiotlb_sync_single_for_device() and
swiotlb_sync_single_for_cpu() call their __swiotlb_*() counterparts under
"if (unlikely(pool))", where pool comes from swiotlb_find_pool(), a stub
returning NULL without CONFIG_SWIOTLB, in which case the __swiotlb_*()
functions are not built either.  An optimizing compiler propagates the
NULL and drops the calls; a compiler that keeps them (tinycc, or gcc -O0)
fails the link of kernel/dma/mapping.o with undefined references on a
configuration without SWIOTLB (32-bit x86).

Test the option directly: IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SWIOTLB) && unlikely(pool).
No change for configurations with SWIOTLB.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 include/linux/swiotlb.h | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/swiotlb.h b/include/linux/swiotlb.h
index 2a421241b..1ad894323 100644
--- a/include/linux/swiotlb.h
+++ b/include/linux/swiotlb.h
@@ -258,7 +258,12 @@ static inline void swiotlb_tbl_unmap_single(struct device *dev,
 {
 	struct io_tlb_pool *pool = swiotlb_find_pool(dev, addr);
 
-	if (unlikely(pool))
+	/*
+	 * Without CONFIG_SWIOTLB swiotlb_find_pool() is a stub returning
+	 * NULL and __swiotlb_*() are not built: test the option directly so
+	 * that the calls are dead code for every compiler.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SWIOTLB) && unlikely(pool))
 		__swiotlb_tbl_unmap_single(dev, addr, size, dir, attrs, pool);
 }
 
@@ -270,7 +275,7 @@ static inline void swiotlb_sync_single_for_device(struct device *dev,
 {
 	struct io_tlb_pool *pool = swiotlb_find_pool(dev, addr);
 
-	if (unlikely(pool))
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SWIOTLB) && unlikely(pool))
 		__swiotlb_sync_single_for_device(dev, addr, size, dir, pool);
 }
 
@@ -282,7 +287,7 @@ static inline void swiotlb_sync_single_for_cpu(struct device *dev,
 {
 	struct io_tlb_pool *pool = swiotlb_find_pool(dev, addr);
 
-	if (unlikely(pool))
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SWIOTLB) && unlikely(pool))
 		__swiotlb_sync_single_for_cpu(dev, addr, size, dir, pool);
 }
 
